From 81eb1c95c671dbe5cba778f96e265dc364ff1812 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kush J <kushisthecoolest@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:48:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Live-test diagnostic: dump Remix's interop output on the RTX
 5070

Investigating a report that the Minecraft window shows vanilla sky +
HUD only, no path-traced output, during an in-game run. Verified
before changing anything: a VK->GL draw path already exists (GlInterop
.waitForVk consumes the semaphore, TextureOverlay.render draws the
color texture full-screen onto client.getFramebuffer(), wired through
GameRendererMixin -> RtxRemixMod.submitRemixFrameIfReady ->
RemixRenderer.blitVkImageToGL) -- the originally-suspected gap
(copyFromFramebuffer returning early) is the *other* direction
(GL->VK, used to feed GUI content into Remix's own compositing) and
its early-return on Linux is intentional (Remix already has its own
output; see the comment on GlInterop.copyFromFramebuffer).

Added InteropTextureDumper: a one-shot PPM dump of the imported color
texture, 15 real seconds after it first becomes available, to check
whether Remix is producing a lit image at all, independent of whatever
composites (or fails to composite) it on screen.

Live result on the RTX 5070 (build/distributions/rtx-remix-renderer-
0.1.0-202610270045-bfa5a51-dirty-linux64.jar, Creative singleplayer,
"New World", existing save): the dumped texture is the correct size
(1253x1352, matching the window) with no GL errors, but is uniformly
black (avg=0.0, min=0, max=0) -- both with default shader-compilation
settings and with RTX_ENABLE_ASYNC_COMPILATION=0 (which fixed an
identical symptom in a synthetic FD-interop test earlier this session;
it did not fix it here). A screenshot taken at the same point shows
exactly vanilla sky, a block-selection wireframe, and the hotbar --
consistent with the dump: there is nothing lit for the existing draw
path to composite.

No "narrow fix" was made to GlInterop/LinuxPresent/RemixRenderer/
RenderSystemMixin: the existing on-screen draw path was not the
problem this session found, so changing it would not have been
verifiable against anything. gradlew is intentionally NOT included in
this commit; the working copy's local gradlew fix is environment-
specific, not part of the mod.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Kush J <kushisthecoolest@gmail.com>
